    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create the specified Python files with the required AWS integrations for image analysis. Each scored implementation file will use a specific AWS service for its functionality. The local helper files will provide utilities for configuration and request/response handling. Here's the plan:\n\n1. Create `detect_image_labels.py` using AWS Rekognition to detect labels in an image.\n2. Create `describe_image.py` using AWS Rekognition to generate a visual description of an image.\n3. Create `detect_image_text.py` using AWS Rekognition to detect text in an image.\n4. Create `score_image_safety.py` using AWS Rekognition to check for unsafe content in an image.\n5. Create `vision_client.py` to provide configuration and client utilities for AWS Rekognition.\n6. Create `vision_models.py` to define request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS Rekognition.\n7. Create `image_summary.py` to summarize visual analysis results.\n8. Create `alt_text_translate.py` to translate generated image descriptions.\n9. Create `visual_safety_text.py` to check generated visual labels for unsafe text.\n10. Create `image_asset_archive.py` to archive image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage. </thinking>\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789842621486,
          "start": 1789842609939
        },
